    {
      "path": "/summary",
      "value": "Business Analyst with around 14+ years career in Information Technology (IT) within the Corporate Banking Payments (ISO 20022), Collections and Receivables. (Cash Management System) and Banking Products Pricing & Billing. Adept in BA practices along with running workshops, requirements elicitation, handling internal and external stakeholders Proficient in creating documents - Functional Requirements documents, Impact Analysis (IA), Gap Analysis, Use Case Documents, User Story, Non-Functional Requirement Extensive work experience in SDLC, Agile, Waterfall methodology Intense working experience in functional testing, system integration (SIT), User acceptance (UAT), and writing complex SQL queries Good understanding of business process flows and requirements management along with excellent analytical, inter-personal, writing skills, facilitating meetings, backlog management, business requirement elicitation, API features and data analysis Exposure to Product Owner roles & responsibilities Working experience on Collection and Receivable, Pricing and Billing and Corporate Payments Working experience on ISO 20022 payment message formats (PACS, PAIN & Cancellation message formats) Ensured adherence to industry standards and regulatory requirements, including 20022, to maintain compliance and security in payment systems Closely worked with stakeholders (Country local clearing, Operations, Compliance, IT, Product) to understand the business and regulatory requirements and understand on how new fields like UETR, structured remittance info, etc., affect internal systems Documented detailed functional and non-functional requirements and analyze the impact of ISO 20022 on existing system, formats (e.g., MT103 Pacs.008) and workflows Created message mapping documents: MT to MX (e.g., MT101 Pain.001, MT103 Pacs.008) and work with XML schemas (XSDs) to validate the ISO 20022 message structure and ensure compliance Supported internal training for OPS/Tech teams on ISO message formats and flows and acted as a subject matter expert (SME) for queries on ISO 20022 structure, tags, and usage rules",
